 35   c  TITL$Nuclear Structure and Decay Data for A=35 Isobars                 
 35   c  AUTH$LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN                                            
 35   c  INST$Facility for Rare Isotope Beams, Michigan State University, East  
 35  2c  Lansing, MI 48824, USA                                                 
 35   c  ABST$This work presents a comprehensive and critical evaluation of     
 35  2c  experimental nuclear spectroscopic data from reactions and decays for  
 35  3c  all 11 known nuclides with mass number 35 (Ne, Na, Mg, Al, Si, P, S,   
 35  4c  Cl, Ar, K, Ca). Recommended values are produced for level energies,    
 35  5c  spins and parities, half-lives, and radiation properties including     
 35  6c  energies, branching ratios, and multipolarities of |g rays, as well as 
 35  7c  characteristics of |b radiation decays, based on a rigorous assessment 
 35  8c  of all available experimental data. Discrepancies among existing       
 35  9c  results are carefully addressed. This work supersedes earlier full     
 35  Ac  evaluations of A=35 published by 2011Ch48, 1990En08 (also 1998En04     
 35  Bc  update) and 1978En02.                                                  
 35  #c
 35  #c  {+35}Cl remains the most extensively studied nuclide, investigated     
 35  2c  through 28 different reactions and decays, followed by {+35}S, {+35}P, 
 35  3c  and {+35}Ar. For {+35}Na, only two excited states have been observed,  
 35  4c  and its |b{+-}-decay scheme has not yet been established. For {+35}Mg, 
 35  5c  no |g rays have been placed with certainty, and no decay dataset exists
 35  6c  on {+35}Mg|){+35}Al. {+35}Ar resonances of astrophysical interest have 
 35  7c  been studied via transfer reactions and {+35}K |e+|b{++} decays, but   
 35  8c  their properties are yet to be determined. For {+35}K, many excited    
 35  9c  states discovered via {+35}Ca |e+|b{++} decay are unresolved. For      
 35  Ac  {+35}Ca, no |g rays have been observed and only one excited state has  
 35  Bc  been identified. Notably, {+35}Ca is the only nuclide in this mass     
 35  Cc  chain that decays by |e+|b{++}-delayed two protons, although the       
 35  Dc  emission mechanism remains unclear.                                    
 35   c  CUT$Literature available up to September 30, 2025 has been consulted,  
 35  2c  with the help of the primary bibliographic source, the NSR database    
 35  3c  (2014Pr09) available at Brookhaven National Laboratory web page:       
 35  4c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/                                                  
 35   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 35  2c  is carried out through a suite of current versions of computer codes   
 35  3c  available at the IAEA-NDS web page of ENSDF codes                      
 35  4c  (https://www-nds.iaea.org/public/ensdf_pgm) such as GLSC, Java-RULER,  
 35  5c  BrIccMixing, and ConsistencyCheck. The direct feedings to excited      
 35  6c  states in |b{+-} and |e decays have generally been computed from       
 35  7c  I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each level; the associated log {Ift}    
 35  8c  values are calculated using the BetaShape code. Theoretical total      
 35  9c  conversion coefficients are calculated using version v2.3e of BrIcc    
 35  Ac  code (2008Ki07) for frozen-orbit option with an implicit uncertainty of
 35  Bc  1.4% when not stated. Q values and particle separation energies have   
 35  Cc  been adopted from 2021Wa16 (AME2020). Static magnetic dipole moments   
 35  Dc  are taken from 2019StZV (long-lived states) and 2020StZV (short-lived  
 35  Ec  states) evaluations, and static electric quadrupole moments from       
 35  Fc  2021StZZ evaluation, when available in these publications. Nuclear rms 
 35  Gc  charge radii have been adopted from 2013An02 evaluation. In cases where
 35  Hc  weighted averaging procedures have been used, the assigned uncertainty 
 35  Ic  in the result is generally not lower than the lowest uncertainty in the
 35  Jc  data points used in the procedure.                                     
 35   c  ACKN$Earlier evaluations (2011Ch48, 1998En04 update, 1990En08,         
